## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design incremental spectral methods for dynamic graphs and reason about trade-offs between update time, accuracy, and memory.

## Key Concepts

- Eigenvector centrality; Rayleigh quotient
- Low-rank updates; batch dynamics
- Subspace iteration; spectral gap
- Complexity trade-offs; memory vs accuracy

## Code Example

```javascript
// simplified incremental update
function updateCentrality(X, A, DeltaA, touched) {
  const Y = project(DeltaA, X);
  X = orthonormalize(X.add(DeltaA.dot(X)));
  return X;
}
```

